# ---- data: regenerate with scripts/01–03, never committed ----
data/raw/*
data/interim/*
data/processed/*
!data/**/.gitkeep

# ---- large binaries ----
*.bin
*.npy
*.npz

# ---- cached agent generations ----
# scripts/14_run_agents.py caches every generation so the evaluation can be
# re-run without a GPU. Regenerable from the checkpoint, and large.
experiments/agents/*.pt

# ---- run outputs ----
# Every run writes experiments/<run>/manifest.json. Those reach the repository
# through scripts/10_collect_results.py, which copies the ones worth keeping
# into results/. Committing experiments/ as well would mean two copies that
# drift apart, and would let a local smoke run masquerade as a result.
experiments/

# ---- the generated benchmark ----
# val and test ARE committed: they are what the results are measured on, and a
# reviewer must be able to check them. train.jsonl is 64 MB and regenerates
# exactly from seed 1337 in about two minutes, so it is not.
data/synth/train.jsonl

# ---- checkpoints ----
# Nothing under checkpoints/ is committed by default. Two reasons, and the
# first is the important one:
#
#   1. A checkpoint written by a local smoke run looks exactly like one from
#      the real training run. Committing by default is how a development
#      artefact ends up presented as the project's model.
#   2. Config B with optimiser state is ~140 MB, over GitHub's 100 MB limit.
#      scripts/17_export_weights.py strips the optimiser state to ~49 MB,
#      which fits; that export is what gets released.
#
# Review 1's ckpt_A_final.pt is the single exception, re-allowed below,
# because it is small and is the artefact that milestone is judged on.
checkpoints/*
!checkpoints/.gitkeep
!checkpoints/ckpt_A_final.pt
checkpoints/*.tmp

# ---- python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
venv/
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
